# ── Ripple Good — environment ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env.local for development. .env* is gitignored; never commit real
# values. Everything with a VITE_ prefix is compiled into the public bundle and
# is readable by anyone — only put things here that are safe in public.

# ── Public (ships in the bundle, by design) ──────────────────────────────────

# Supabase project URL and anon key. The anon key is meant to be public: row
# level security denies it every row of donation_events, and the only thing it
# may call is the donation_totals() aggregate function.
# Leave both unset and the site builds and runs exactly as before, with no
# verified totals shown.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Every.org's donate-link "webhook_token". Public by construction — it rides in
# the donate URL, so treat it as a correlator, never as a credential.
VITE_EVERYORG_LINK_TOKEN=

# ── Server-side only (NEVER prefix these with VITE_) ─────────────────────────
# Set with: supabase secrets set NAME=value
#
# EVERYORG_URL_SECRET        The real guard on the webhook endpoint. A long
#                            random string that appears only in the URL you
#                            paste into Every.org's developer dashboard:
#                              https://<ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/everyorg-webhook?k=<secret>
#                            Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
#
# EVERYORG_WEBHOOK_TOKEN     Same value as VITE_EVERYORG_LINK_TOKEN. Only used
#                            to log mismatches; not trusted.
#
# SUPABASE_URL               Injected automatically by Supabase Edge Functions.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  Injected automatically. Bypasses RLS. Never expose.
#
# ── Donation alerts (all optional; set one group or none) ────────────────────
# The webhook pings you once per new donation. Whichever group is set below
# wins, in this order; set none and no alert is sent, which is the default.
#
# The alert carries the amount, the cause and the nonprofit. It cannot carry
# donor details: it is built from the stored row, and the row has none.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY             Email, via Resend. Pair with ALERT_EMAIL_TO.
# ALERT_EMAIL_TO             Where the alert goes.
# ALERT_EMAIL_FROM           Optional. Defaults to onboarding@resend.dev, which
#                            works before any domain is verified. Once you
#                            verify ripple-good.org with Resend, set this to
#                            something like alerts@ripple-good.org.
#
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL        Discord channel webhook. No signup beyond Discord.
#
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN         Telegram, via a bot from @BotFather.
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID           Your own chat id.
#
# ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL          Anything else that accepts a JSON POST. Sends
#                            {text, amountCents, causeId, ...}; Slack-shaped.
